What this licence covers, and what it does not.

Covers: the project's own source, tools, tests, build scripts and
documentation -- everything in this repository that the project authored,
unless a file or directory says otherwise. Third-party components keep their
own licences; see THIRD-PARTY.md.

Does not cover:

  * Tokimeki Memorial: Forever with You. The game, its code, its data, its
    art, its music and its text are (c) Konami. This repository holds no disc
    images and none of the game's data files, Japanese script text, art,
    audio or video.
    The disc-derived inputs are built on your machine from your own copy
    (docs/GETTING-STARTED.md). The repository does contain the project's
    reimplementation in C (below), symbol maps, decompiled C for the Sony
    SDK functions linked into the game, initial values of some program
    variables, and a small amount of disassembly quoted in documentation.
    The MIT grant covers only the project's own expression in these. It
    grants no right in the game, and the project claims none.
  * Trademarks. "Tokimeki Memorial" is a trademark of Konami; "PlayStation"
    is a trademark of Sony Interactive Entertainment. This is an unofficial
    fan project, not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Konami or
    Sony. Neither this licence nor the project grants any trademark right.
  * The reception of this repository as a decompilation. The C sources under
    src/ are the project's own expression of the game's behaviour, written to
    be byte-identical to the retail build; they are not a copy of Konami's
    source, and the project makes no claim about Konami's rights in the
    original work.
  * The vendored third-party directories listed in THIRD-PARTY.md, which carry
    their own terms.